# Lean token usage

Treat context as scarce. Target staying under ~10% of the window unless the task truly needs more.

## Do

- Prefer `rg`/path jumps over broad repo dumps; read only the lines you need.
- Cap tool output (`head`, offsets, small limits). Don’t re-read files you already have.
- Parallelize only when it saves rounds; skip exploratory subagents for simple edits.
- Keep replies short: answer + links/actions; no process narrations or repeated summaries.
- One focused PR/change set; avoid drive-by refactors and extra markdown.

## Don’t

- Paste large logs/JSON/HTML into chat; summarize or cite paths.
- Dump full files “for context” when a symbol/range is enough.
- Restate AGENTS.md/rules the user already knows.
- Open long-running explore agents for needle lookups.

If stuck, ask one tight question instead of scanning the whole repo.
